WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.119 --> 00:00:05.790
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, this morning
I asked you all to submit Doctor Who questions

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.029
so this video will be all about those.

00:00:08.029 --> 00:00:11.969
Most of you are really curious about Capaldi’s
catchphrase or big characters returning.

00:00:11.969 --> 00:00:14.599
Thankfully Moffat has explained a little about
some of this that I’ll mention when we get

00:00:14.599 --> 00:00:15.599
going.

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:17.180
Quick congrats to Brad Miller, you’re this
week’s giveaway winner.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:18.180
It’s an amazon giftcard.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.330
I’ll message you on your channel for details.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:24.170
Next round of the giveaway starts when I post
my Classic Who video later this week.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.930
That might end up being Saturday, maybe sooner
if I can get through a few other videos.

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:32.809
Remember all you have to do to enter is be
a subscriber and leave a comment.

00:00:32.809 --> 00:00:37.300
So on to questions, Number 1 - The Doctor’s
Assistant asks What was your first episode

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.890
of Doctor Who?

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:43.440
The first one I can remember consiously planning
on watching was Eleventh Hour the first time

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.440
it aired.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.260
My family was more Star Wars and Lord of the
Rings growing up so I didn’t discover Doctor

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.170
Who until well after the 2005 reboot.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:53.281
I think it was one of the science fiction
blogs I read at the time hyping it up before

00:00:53.281 --> 00:00:56.569
Matt Smith’s debut so I decided to check
it out and fell in love with it.

00:00:56.569 --> 00:01:03.020
I’ll say that I ended up liking series 6
the most just because the cast had gotten

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:07.300
a lot more comfortable in their clothes so
to speak, they were more of a family and I

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.540
was much more personally invested in the story
at that point.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:13.050
Series 7 felt a bit weird just because of
the big mid-season break.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.110
I think I circled back around to watch Eccleston
and Tennant’s episodes sometime during Series

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:16.110
6.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.110
And then slowly started watching classic who.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.080
There’s still a ton of stuff I haven’t
seen.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.380
But I can very clearly remember what I felt
like, what my apartment looked like, what

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.051
I was thinking about when Eleventh Hour was
getting ready to premiere.

00:01:23.051 --> 00:01:26.810
Question 2 - Keegen Bezenah asks when you
do videos for the episodes could you point

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.380
out easter eggs if you see them?

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:34.500
I’ll definitely try to catch as much as
possible, but the more Classic Who you’ve

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.670
watched the better your chances are for seeing
things.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:41.170
Most of the stuff I mention will probably
be the really clear stuff.

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:45.300
But sometimes Doctor Who actors will make
some subtle choice in a scene that is a reference

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.570
but is so subtle you barely notice it.

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:51.530
I’m trying to figure out a way for you guys
to message me with easter eggs you see that

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:52.530
I missed.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:54.970
If there’s stuff you guys find I want to
give you credit.

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:58.550
So stay tuned, once I think of an organized
way to handle that I’ll let you all know

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:02.680
so you can participate.

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:07.200
Question 3 - Chrisy Smith asks Do you think
that Clara will stick around or will the changes

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.770
scare her off?

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:12.670
I think episode 1 will handle most of the
Clara gets used to Capaldi.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:16.930
The hurdle she has to jump over is the Doctor
not being the Doctor as she knows him.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:18.739
So there relationship has to adapt.

00:02:18.739 --> 00:02:22.849
That might be why Moffat included Vastra in
the episode.

00:02:22.849 --> 00:02:25.920
She’s always been a neutral figure in the
Doctor’s life.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:30.849
Someone who is long-lived like he is and has
a much broader perspective on the matter.

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:34.609
Most companions only know one version of the
Doctor, some get to see the new one after

00:02:34.609 --> 00:02:36.010
the regeneration like Sarah Jane.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:39.700
It will definitely be weird but I think she’ll
adapt pretty fast.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:43.650
Question 4 - Edward asks do you think Clara
will reference Matt Smith’s Doctor a lot

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.990
or is he done and gone?

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:50.469
Yes, she’ll still be thinking Matt Smith
when she’s thinking of the Doctor.

00:02:50.469 --> 00:02:53.290
Capaldi will be like an abstract idea.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:54.769
Like seeing your friend in cosplay.

00:02:54.769 --> 00:02:58.959
I don’t know how long she’ll keep referring
to past events with the Doctor but I think

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:04.810
after the first few episodes she’ll speak
more in present tense and less in past tense.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:08.189
There’s rumors about a Matt Smith phone
call in the first episode.

00:03:08.189 --> 00:03:12.779
If that’s true, that would be the big hurdle
they cross before they get on with their new

00:03:12.779 --> 00:03:13.779
lives.

00:03:13.779 --> 00:03:17.269
There was a clip from episode 2 that’s been
turned into gif’s on tumblr.

00:03:17.269 --> 00:03:21.150
Based on the jokes in that I think that Matt
Smith references will largely be limited to

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.569
the first episode.

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:29.120
But every time the Doctor runs into a character
we haven’t seen for a long time they’ll

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:33.579
probably have that quick moment where the
person isn’t sure who they’re looking

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:35.680
at till the Doctor says something familiar.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:39.620
Question 5 - Cailan Cook asks are there going
to be any Two Parters this year?

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.900
Yes, the finale is two parts.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:47.370
I don’t remember where I saw it but I think
Moffat claimed the stories would be less serialized

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:48.370
this year too.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.870
Meaning there would be more one-off episodes.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.989
It makes sense they’d do that for Capaldi’s
first run.

00:03:51.989 --> 00:03:57.280
It’s a lot easier for new viewers to jump
on a series if they don’t have to know a

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:59.559
lot of details from earlier episodes.

00:03:59.559 --> 00:04:02.739
They kind of did the same thing with series
5.

00:04:02.739 --> 00:04:07.749
Once they got to series 6 though the River
Song Lake Silencio plot took up most of the

00:04:07.749 --> 00:04:08.749
story.

00:04:08.749 --> 00:04:13.540
Question 6 - Mario Hernandez asks do you think
Capaldi will use a lot of previous Doctor’s

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:14.800
catchphrases in the episode?

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:19.280
I’ve heard there’s a very signature Tom
Baker catchphrase but I think he’ll do a

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:24.210
bit from all the Doctor’s, some references
will be more obvious than others but Capaldi’s

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:29.370
Doctor is supposed to be closer to the third
and fourth doctors than any of the others.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:33.410
That will tie in with the easter eggs and
references I was talking about.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:37.850
If you guys see certain things you can just
message me and I’ll add it to my episode

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:38.850
videos.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:44.530
I know a lot of you have been asking what
I think Capaldi’s catchphrase will end up

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:48.200
being and I don’t know but I’d love it
if there was a little bit of Malcolm Tucker

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.200
in it.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:52.230
I don’t think the BBC would let him swear
that much but I think we’ll see some pretty

00:04:52.230 --> 00:05:02.479
amazing tumblr edits when people start posting
gif sets of the episodes.

00:05:02.479 --> 00:05:07.820
Question 7 - Alec Plumley asks I watched Tennant’s
run but do I need to watch Matt Smith’s

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:09.389
run to understand what’s going on?

00:05:09.389 --> 00:05:14.699
Good question, no you don’t but it will
give you a little more context.

00:05:14.699 --> 00:05:19.470
If you don’t have time to watch all of Matt
Smith’s run just watch series 7b through

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:20.729
the christmas special.

00:05:20.729 --> 00:05:24.930
If you really really don’t have any time,
just watch the 50th and the christmas special.

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:27.780
I did post a beginners guide but it’s really
just a cliff’s notes.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:31.639
The truth is you could watch everything and
there would still be the novels, the audio

00:05:31.639 --> 00:05:32.770
dramas and the comics.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:35.030
So you just have to draw the line somewhere.

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:37.250
Really you should at least watch the 50th.

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:39.039
It was amazing.

00:05:39.039 --> 00:05:43.020
Question 8 - Michael Jarvis asks Do you think
we'll see the return of Omega?

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:45.370
I don’t think so, and here’s why.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:47.889
It’s mostly because the old things that
Moffat is bringing back.

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:51.840
Or at least the stuff that we know about right
now.

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:56.819
Is all stuff he’s either written himself
or stuff from his time as showrunner.

00:05:56.819 --> 00:06:01.330
When it comes to classic who I think the things
they’re bringing back are mostly thematic

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:02.770
and visual.

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:06.599
Not so much characters but character traits
and the tone of some of the previous Doctors.

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:10.720
There’s a lot we still don’t know so it’s
always possible, but I think they also want

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:15.030
to introduce some new monsters and villains,
so bringing in someone like Omega would overshadow

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:16.530
any new things they brought in.

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:18.630
I don’t think they want to steal focus too
much.

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:23.160
That’s part of the reason the Master isn’t
coming back, that and scheduling.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:27.099
Remember, John Simm has a new series that
he’s on called intruders.

00:06:27.099 --> 00:06:29.800
It’s premiering right after Deep Breath
premieres.

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:34.050
Question 9 - James McQueen asks what’s your
favorite TARDIS interior?

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:38.270
I always like new interiors, so each time
I see a new one I think it’s better.

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:41.729
But if I had to pick I’d say the one I was
most excited about was John Hurt’s TARDIS.

00:06:41.729 --> 00:06:46.990
He was billed as the War Doctor so I got so
hyped to see what a TARDIS would look like

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:48.500
during the Time War.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:52.610
The Doctor changed himself to be more brutal
so his console would fit that personality

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:53.610
and function.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:58.240
It looked like a colder version of 9’s TARDIS
with the Round Things.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:01.849
I really loved that scene where Smith and
Tennant were trying to remember what the purpose

00:07:01.849 --> 00:07:04.449
of the Round Things were and couldn’t figure
it out.

00:07:04.449 --> 00:07:08.909
and Question 10 last one - Ejazz Hreidmarr
asks In the 50th Anniversary Tom Baker told

00:07:08.909 --> 00:07:11.500
Matt Smith that he’d be revisiting Old Faces
soon.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:15.139
What do you think that means and are they
going to follow up on it in series 8?

00:07:15.139 --> 00:07:17.610
I think it could mean two things.

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:23.849
First seeing old faces as in Old Doctor’s
faces again in the next anniversary special.

00:07:23.849 --> 00:07:30.110
I think we can all agree it was awesome seeing
Tom Baker show up and the 5ish Doctors short.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:33.800
So he was talking about them coming back literally.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:42.009
And I also think he was talking about Capaldi,
who we had not met yet.

00:07:42.009 --> 00:07:46.340
Capaldi talks about his face being familiar
and somehow mysterious, like when he looks

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:51.249
in the mirror he recognizes the face as a
face he’s seen before but can’t place

00:07:51.249 --> 00:07:52.249
it.

00:07:52.249 --> 00:07:54.280
I think that will be one of the running plots
this series.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:58.419
Finding out if the Doctor is re-using an old
face and if he is, why.

00:07:58.419 --> 00:08:02.250
What’s the purpose in re-using a face versus
picking a new face.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:04.249
All great questions, thank you for leaving
them.

00:08:04.249 --> 00:08:08.749
Since I’ll have more time for bonus videos
eventually I’ll try to do more questions

00:08:08.749 --> 00:08:09.749
in the future.

00:08:09.749 --> 00:08:12.150
Like 15 or 20 versus 10.

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:14.789
Like I said, my next video will be the Classic
Who one.

00:08:14.789 --> 00:08:16.939
I’ll try to post that by Saturday if not
earlier.

00:08:16.939 --> 00:08:18.310
I have jury duty friday, yay.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:21.060
So we’ll see.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:29.319
In the meantime click here for my beginner’s
guide if you haven’t seen it and click here

00:08:29.319 --> 00:08:32.150
to learn about the new trailer and all of
the episode titles this season.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:34.459
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:08:34.459 --> 00:08:35.229
High Fives!

